LUMA SUMMARY:
Deep diagnostic of MMRC response stability. The team isolates two core parser issues: repeated DOM reads and a weak stability test that was accepting delimiter presence instead of a stable candidate. They converge on passing one verified candidate through the wait/extraction path, comparing exact candidate snapshots across polls, and keeping protocol delimiters strictly structural. The session ends with a small, testable root-cause fix rather than a redesign.
